      "image": null,
      "content": "An AI agent can ace an isolated benchmark and still break critical business workflows within minutes of deployment. Unlike standard text models that output static completions, autonomous agents execute tool calls, mutate database states, and trigger irreversible side effects across your infrastructure.\n\nEvaluating these systems requires looking beyond final accuracy metrics. A robust production harness must isolate the agent trajectory across four distinct planes: dataset generation without existing production traffic, runtime execution environment controls, intermediate trajectory verification, and holistic cost-per-step scoring.\n\nTool execution drift, unconstrained prompt retries, and API schema divergence often derail an agent long before the underlying foundational model makes a reasoning mistake. Verifying state transitions step-by-step is the only way to safeguard systems that issue real writes to systems of record.\n\nReliable agents demand rigor in intermediate behavior, not blind faith in end-to-end evaluation scores."
    },
    {
