      "content": "Running distributed observability platforms often demands maintaining complex clusters for telemetry ingestion, indexing, and analytics. Pitot simplifies this architecture into a single binary.\n\nThe system accepts standard OpenTelemetry (OTLP) payloads over gRPC and HTTP, persists the incoming traces, metrics, and logs into columnar Parquet files, and executes analytical queries on demand using DuckDB. It eliminates the need for separate Elasticsearch, ClickHouse, or Prometheus clusters in local or medium-scale environments.\n\nIn addition to local embedded storage, Pitot integrates an MCP (Model Context Protocol) server interface. This permits local reasoning models or debugging agents to introspect telemetry data programmatically via structured SQL over DuckDB.\n\nReplacing multi-tier ingest infrastructure with native columnar files and an embedded query engine provides a practical, low-overhead blueprint for developer sandboxes and edge deployments."
