      "content": "Modifying real-time streaming pipelines often forces engineers to fork foundational networking libraries. Pion addresses this architectural friction with its Interceptor design pattern in Go.\n\nDrawing direct inspiration from GStreamer pipelines, the Interceptor API establishes a composable middleware chain around RTP and RTCP packets. Developers can hook directly into inbound reader and outbound writer streams without modifying core peer connection logic.\n\nEach interceptor lifecycle hooks into stream binding events, receiving contextual stream metadata before handling raw packet batches. This decoupled structure allows custom jitter buffers, NACK generators, bandwidth estimators, and custom encryption wrappers to chain together cleanly.\n\nFor engineers designing distributed media gateways or real-time networking protocols, this modular middleware blueprint demonstrates how to keep core transport mechanics isolated from application-specific packet transformations."
